  "description": "<p>The University of Hartford is a private university in West Hartford, Connecticut. Founded in 1877, the university is divided into seven schools and colleges and is noted for its narrow student-to-faculty ratio of 9:1 that allows students quality time with the expert professors employed at the university.</p><p>Over 100 programs in numerous fields of study are available at different levels, from undergraduate to graduate and beyond.</p><h2>What is the University of Hartford acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The University of Hartford acceptance rate is 78%.</p> <p>The University of Hartford has a range of facilities open to students, including the Allen library and the Mortensen library. Access to books, journals and other resources are all readily available in an ambient setting. Every classroom and lab is equipped with modern technology and empowers students to expand their knowledge. First-rate wellness and sports centers are also for students to stay healthy and active, with access to a swimming pool and other recreational activities readily available.</p><p>Men's and womenâ€™s basketball teams and the Al-Marzook field are just some notable athletics facilities students can enjoy while studying at the university.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Campus life is diverse and gives students many opportunities to learn and socialize. There are over 100 organizations for students to choose from, ensuring a wide variety of interests are covered. Numerous events and activities are free to attend during the year, including lectures, concerts and cultural festivals. Famous artists perform at the annual event held in the fall season on campus. Various fast food outlets and cafes are dotted around campus for students to enjoy a bite to eat. Various community initiatives ensure students can come together for a good cause.</p><p>The University of Hartford also has an active sports team called the Hawks, and there are athletics opportunities such as soccer, basketball, lacrosse and more.</p>",
