  "highlights": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "value": "<p>The University of Hartford is a private university in West Hartford, Connecticut. Founded in 1877, the university is divided into seven schools and colleges and is noted for its narrow student-to-faculty ratio of 9:1 that allows students quality time with the expert professors employed at the university.</p><p>Over 100 programs in numerous fields of study are available at different levels, from undergraduate to graduate and beyond.</p><p>Men's and women's basketball teams and the Al-Marzook field are just some notable athletics facilities students can enjoy while studying at the university.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>A variety of accommodations is available at the University of Hartford. Traditional residence halls are available for freshmen to mix together that contain a choice of living arrangements, including dormitory-style rooms and suites. Apartment-style housing options are similarly available for senior students that can be selected according to different size capacities, from one-bedroom to three-bedroom options.</p><p>Special interest housing might be an area of interest for students coming to the university too, such as wellness-themed housing and halls designated for honours students. Students are encouraged to scope out all available living arrangements and compare them against their overall eligibility prior to commencing their studies.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p>First-rate wellness and sports centers are also for students to stay healthy and active, with access to a swimming pool and other recreational activities readily available.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lab",
      "value": "<p>Every classroom and lab is equipped with modern technology and empowers students to expand their knowledge.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>The University of Hartford has a range of facilities open to students, including the Allen library and the Mortensen library. Access to books, journals and other resources are all readily available in an ambient setting.&nbsp;</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>Campus life is diverse and gives students many opportunities to learn and socialize. There are over 100 organizations for students to choose from, ensuring a wide variety of interests are covered. Numerous events and activities are free to attend during the year, including lectures, concerts and cultural festivals. Famous artists perform at the annual event held in the fall season on campus. Various fast food outlets and cafes are dotted around campus for students to enjoy a bite to eat. Various community initiatives ensure students can come together for a good cause.</p><p>The University of Hartford also has an active sports team called the Hawks, and there are athletics opportunities such as soccer, basketball, lacrosse and more.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    }
